<section image-layout="blank" id="BblFLMzy0S" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="wLbH1828G7" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Ozone policy · The exposure atlas</p><h1 font-size="44pt">The risk is concentrated—and often poorly mapped</h1><p font-size="lg">Committee thesis: ozone policy is a targeted diligence issue—not a broad green-premium story. Map substance-dependent assets, separate legacy ozone-depleting substances from HFC climate exposure, then test transition capex, operating resilience and management evidence against valuation.</p><spacer size="24pt"></spacer><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="xs"><p font-size="sm">Investment committee briefing · Exposure atlas</p></grid-item><grid-item id="YjKjeNyR-t" padding="0" colspan="24"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/wHnkhVXJiuFksl97P2xAz.png" saved-media-id="cupvvlggk7n080u" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="industrial-atmospheric-relief" alt="Precision editorial relief construction of atmospheric layers intersecting with a refrigeration compressor, cooling coil, recovery cylinder and valves, built from matte mineral paper and oxidized metal under cool raking studio light, exposure blue, transition teal, restrained rust accents and charcoal shadows, no text, no lettering, no logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="eSTVyqpTmT"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="GnrWcibA7l" vertical-align="center" colspan="38"><h2>One recovery story, two different refrigerant issues</h2><p>Stratospheric ozone absorbs harmful ultraviolet radiation. The Montreal Protocol phases out ozone-depleting substances.</p><grid divider="sm neutral-border" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="oST6uBR6Ty" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">2040</display><h4>Global</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="l3NSZ-53mU" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">2045</display><h4>Arctic</h4></grid-item><grid-item id="Vc8xvPqi2S" vertical-align="center" colspan="20"><display size="md">2066</display><h4>Antarctica</h4></grid-item></grid><p font-size="sm"><b>Projected return to 1980 ozone levels—if current policies remain.</b></p><aside variant="info"><p><b>Keep separate:</b> HFCs warm the climate but do not deplete ozone. The Kigali Amendment is related, but scientifically and policy-distinct.</p></aside><p role="caption">Sources: <a href="https://www.unep.org/news-and-stories/press-release/ozone-layer-recovery-track-helping-avoid-global-warming-05degc">UNEP 2023 assessment summary</a>; <a href="https://ozone.unep.org/treaties/montreal-protocol">Montreal Protocol</a>.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="dGMReiSQ9I" padding="0" colspan="22"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/gADT1E7M2xArfmm0FEgym.png" saved-media-id="hrz3589y8ki6rl2" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="industrial-atmospheric-relief" alt="Precision editorial relief cross-section of layered stratosphere above an abstract refrigeration system, a compressor and coiled tubing connected beneath translucent mineral-paper atmospheric bands, oxidized metal details, cool raking light, exposure blue and transition teal with one restrained rust signal, no text, no lettering, no logos" meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="VlAQY5vsx0" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="5Sl7IEHByP"><h2>Map equipment and substances before mapping sectors</h2><p>For each holding, establish five coordinates before concluding on exposure.</p><grid marker="number" marker-rule="true" marker-position="above" marker-align="start" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="hug" style="--marker-gap: 0.6em;"><grid-item id="8tHC9PgT6x" colspan="12"><h4>Substance</h4><p>ODS, HFC, lower-impact substitute, or unknown.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="SV8selxd90" colspan="12"><h4>Asset</h4><p>Refrigeration, HVAC, foam, fire suppression, or industrial process.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="G2W5GljSTR" colspan="12"><h4>Lifecycle</h4><p>Installation, servicing, replacement, recovery, or disposal.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="J7AlM0nf-E" colspan="12"><h4>Value channel</h4><p>Capex, operating cost, downtime, compliance, or customer access.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="lW3pQhaoBY" colspan="12"><h4>Action</h4><p>Underwrite, reserve, engage, monitor, or defer.</p></grid-item></grid><aside><p><b>Investment implication:</b> a sector label cannot substitute for equipment and substance evidence.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="WDsoujL6-S" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="r_89BvvHDG"><h2>Policy reaches value through physical systems</h2><p>Move from policy to valuation only through a validated transmission chain.</p><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="chevron" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-fill="true" spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug" padding="1em" style="--marker-chip-padding: 0.75em;"><grid-item id="0KM0NVXwt-" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Substance + asset</p><h4>Policy scope</h4><p>Identify the relevant substance, use and jurisdiction.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="R6ANQnK9U6" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Lifecycle</p><h4>Operational constraint</h4><p>Test equipment, servicing, supply and end-of-life handling.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="nO4yM6OwjB" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Value channel</p><h4>Financial transmission</h4><p>Test capex, maintenance, downtime, working capital and margins.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="3ge3ABMSp1" colspan="15"><p role="eyebrow">Action</p><h4>Valuation response</h4><p>Adjust only when exposure and timing are evidenced.</p></grid-item></grid><aside variant="warning"><p>Unknown substance inventories reduce underwriting confidence before they prove financial loss.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="VtBnZfD_1x"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="V1SnVOAtTh"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative example · Not portfolio data</p><h2>Illustrative portfolio matrix: urgency × materiality</h2><freeform-block w="840" h="290"><box type="content" x="90" y="15" w="355" h="118" sizing="fixed" locked="true" background-color="rgba(45,111,142,0.06)"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="445" y="15" w="355" h="118" sizing="fixed" locked="true" background-color="rgba(182,78,60,0.10)"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="90" y="133" w="355" h="117" sizing="fixed" locked="true" background-color="rgba(93,102,107,0.04)"><p></p></box><box type="content" x="445" y="133" w="355" h="117" sizing="fixed" locked="true" background-color="rgba(40,122,114,0.06)"><p></p></box><shape preset="line" x="90" y="250" w="710" h="2" locked="true" stroke="neutral-border" stroke-width="2"></shape><shape preset="line" x="90" y="15" w="2" h="235" locked="true" stroke="neutral-border" stroke-width="2"></shape><box type="content" x="2" y="18" w="78"><p font-size="11pt" align="right"><b>HIGH</b><br>financial materiality</p></box><box type="content" x="4" y="215" w="76"><p font-size="11pt" align="right"><b>LOW</b></p></box><box type="content" x="92" y="258" w="170"><p font-size="11pt">LOW transition urgency</p></box><box type="content" x="625" y="258" w="175"><p font-size="11pt" align="right">HIGH transition urgency</p></box><box type="content" x="595" y="34" w="195" h="74" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-2" style="padding: 8pt 10pt;"><h4 font-size="13pt">ACT NOW · ODS</h4><p font-size="11pt">Legacy-ODS cold store · 4/5 urgency · 4/5 impact<br><b>Reserve + engage</b></p></box><box type="content" x="360" y="57" w="215" h="84" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-3" style="padding: 8pt 10pt;"><h4 font-size="13pt">PLAN · HFC</h4><p font-size="11pt">HFC-heavy supermarket estate · 3/5 urgency · 4/5 impact<br>Climate exposure; not ozone depletion.</p></box><box type="content" x="360" y="164" w="215" h="74" sizing="fixed" background-color="palette-1" style="padding: 8pt 10pt;"><h4 font-size="13pt">VERIFY · UNKNOWN</h4><p font-size="11pt">Older fire suppression · 3/5 urgency · 2/5 impact<br><b>Defer if material</b></p></box><box type="content" x="105" y="190" w="220" h="58" sizing="fixed" background-color="surface" style="padding: 7pt 10pt;"><h4 font-size="13pt">MONITOR · INDIRECT</h4><p font-size="11pt">Landlord-controlled HVAC · 1/5 urgency · 1/5 impact</p></box></freeform-block><p role="caption">Scores and holdings are illustrative replacements—not portfolio data. Confirm all five coordinates before assigning underwrite, reserve, engage, monitor, or defer.</p></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="APEXmRzCFA" vertical-align="center"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="S58uhxmeyA"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative assumptions · Not forecasts</p><h2>Stress the transition, not the recovery forecast</h2><p>Apply these sensitivities only after validating the equipment and substance inventory.</p><grid spacing="medium" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="wZVRIv60GP" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="outline">Base</label></labels><h3>Planned replacement</h3><ul><li>Planned replacement cycle</li><li>Servicing cost +5%</li><li>No incremental downtime</li></ul></grid-item><grid-item id="RhRESiRTjy" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="solid">Tighter transition</label></labels><h3>Earlier capex</h3><ul><li>Replacement three years earlier</li><li>Capex +12%</li><li>Transition-year EBITDA margin −1 percentage point</li></ul></grid-item><grid-item id="cT1m56oiqs" cell-style="subtle" colspan="20"><labels><label variant="solid">Supply disruption</label></labels><h3>Capacity pressure</h3><ul><li>Equipment lead time +6 months</li><li>Servicing cost +20%</li><li>Temporary capacity constraint</li></ul></grid-item></grid><aside><p>Revalue with issuer-specific timing, contracts and financing capacity.</p></aside></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="5eNqILnn-0"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="6XcDyb3DBT"><h2>Minimum evidence for an investable transition plan</h2><p>The plan becomes investable when the exposure map, operating records and funded response reconcile.</p><grid spacing="large" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="P4ijkQsSmf" colspan="37"><h3>Minimum evidence pack</h3><grid divider="sm neutral-border" marker="number" marker-style="subtle" marker-shape="rounded" marker-position="inline" marker-numbering-format="decimal-leading-zero" direction="vertical" vertical-sizing="fill" style="--marker-inline-size: 30pt; --marker-gap: 12pt;"><grid-item id="bj0FmaUHHQ" padding="10pt 0"><p>Inventory by substance, equipment, location, age and ownership.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="f142SU9NlP" padding="10pt 0"><p>Leak, maintenance, servicing, recovery and disposal records.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="ta6cv7sg6j" padding="10pt 0"><p>Replacement schedule, approved capex, suppliers and technician capacity.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="6U6MJK8Oed" padding="10pt 0"><p>Scenario ownership and board-level accountability.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="Lryg7gN9ea" colspan="23"><h3>Decision gates</h3><grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill"><grid-item id="9uRMDkkYuv" background-color="palette-3"><h4>Underwrite</h4><p>Inventory and funded plan are credible.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="8vbhS7Zbcl" background-color="palette-1"><h4>Reserve + engage</h4><p>Evidence gaps are bounded and management has an owner.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="BbtQ-fUeSB" background-color="palette-2"><h4>Defer</h4><p>Unknown exposure could be material.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>
<section image-layout="blank" id="ijzyGjGFnA" vertical-align="center" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="qtRpEHi_lu"><p role="eyebrow">Committee decision</p><h1 font-size="38pt">Committee decision: turn unknowns into priced evidence</h1><h3 role="subheading">Approve a 90-day portfolio screen.</h3><grid marker="number" marker-size="large" marker-style="solid" marker-shape="circle" marker-position="above" marker-align="center" marker-straddle="true" spacing="medium" padding-top="28pt"><grid-item id="lMChLylpDx" background-color="surface" colspan="15"><h4>Prioritize assets</h4><p>Screen refrigeration, cooling, foam, fire-suppression and process dependence.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="IBibzDdmbX" background-color="surface" colspan="15"><h4>Classify substance</h4><p>Assign ODS, HFC, lower-impact substitute, or unknown.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="YItiKsKlfe" background-color="surface" colspan="15"><h4>Price the evidence</h4><p>Request the minimum pack and rerun the illustrative stresses.</p></grid-item><grid-item id="gadtcSHIpc" background-color="surface" colspan="15"><h4>Govern escalation</h4><p>Set thresholds, engagement owners and reporting cadence.</p></grid-item></grid><spacer size="14pt"></spacer><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item id="tUjVXhilJU" background-color="palette-2" padding="12pt 16pt"><h3>No substance map, no confident transition valuation.</h3></grid-item></grid></grid-item></grid></section>